    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d596">

                <pb facs="0756" n="742" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg742"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.24/5–1845</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4918</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-18">May 18, 1945</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I enclose for your confidential
                    information a copy of the Department’s note of even date to the Chilean Embassy
                    in Washington, together with a copy of Statement LL–4<anchor n="26"
                        xml:id="d596-f1"/> prepared by the Foreign <pb facs="0757" n="743"
                        xml:id="pg743"/> Economic Administration showing charges made against the
                    Government of Chile during the period from December 1, 1944 through February 28,
                    1945 covering defense matériel transferred in accordance with the terms of the
                    Lend-Lease Agreement signed on March. 2, 1943.<anchor n="26a" xml:id="d596-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>It will be noted that the charges made against Chile through February 28, 1945
                    for all defense matériel transferred in accordance with the Agreement aggregate
                    the grand total of $19,276,192.11. To date, two reimbursement payments on
                    account amounting to a total of $5,000,000 have been received from Chile.</p>
                <p>In this connection, you are informed that henceforth negotiations for effecting
                    lend-lease collections from the other American republics, including Chile, will
                    be conducted here in Washington between officers of the Department and the
                    respective Embassies. The American Missions in the countries concerned will be
                    kept informed of developments.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d596-f3"/> Also, this
                    Government will continue to maintain the policy of requesting reimbursement
                    payments in accordance with the terms stipulated in the Lend-Lease Agreements
                    with the various other American republics.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Acting Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William L. Clayton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d596-f1" n="26" xml:id="d596-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d596-f2" n="26a" xml:id="d596-f2-content">
                <p>For a summary of the Agreement, see <ref target="frus1943v05#pg_816">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1943, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">v</hi>, p. 816</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d596-f3" n="27" xml:id="d596-f3-content">
                <p>Instruction 5131, September 4, 1945, reported additional charges of $11,431.48
                    from March 1 through May 31, 1945, with no additional reimbursement payments
                    (825.24/9–745). See also instruction 5287, December 11, <ref target="#pg753">p.
                        753</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
